        Pakistan&#39;s recent flight-test of its indigenous Fa&#39;az air-to-air missile signals a new push for self-reliance. How does it stack up against Chinese imports and India&#39;s air defense posture? Read our strategic breakdown.
        
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ The Fa&#39;az is being developed by GIDS under NESCOM in two distinct variants: a passive imaging infrared (IIR) version and an active radar-guided (RF) version.
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ Strategic analysts debate the true indigenous depth of the Fa’az, noting potential technological linkages with Turkish defense entities like TÜBİTAK SAGE.
